{"abstract":"Central pattern generators are circuits generating rhythmic movements, such as walking. The majority of existing computational models of these circuits produce antagonistic output where all neurons within a population spike with a broad burst at about the same neuronal phase with respect to network output. However, experimental recordings reveal that many neurons within these circuits fire sparsely, sometimes as rarely as once within a cycle. Here we address the sparse neuronal firing and develop a model to replicate the behavior of individual neurons within rhythm-generating populations to increase biological plausibility and facilitate new insights into the underlying mechanisms of rhythm generation. The developed network architecture is able to produce sparse firing of individual neurons, creating a novel implementation for exploring the contribution of network architecture on rhythmic output. Furthermore, the introduction of sparse firing of individual neurons within the rhythm-generating circuits is one of the factors that allows for a broad neuronal phase representation of firing at the population level. This moves the model toward recent experimental findings of evenly distributed neuronal firing across phases among individual spinal neurons. The network is tested by methodically iterating select parameters to gain an understanding of how connectivity and the interplay of excitation and inhibition influence the output. This knowledge can be applied in future studies to implement a biologically plausible rhythm-generating circuit for testing biological hypotheses.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Strohmer, Beck","Najarro, Elias","Ausborn, Jessica","Berg, Rune W.","Tolu, Silvia"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-735417"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Najarro, Elias","Strohmer, Beck"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Drexel University"],"keyword":["Action Potentials","Animals","Central Pattern Generators","Computer Simulation","Humans","Models Neurological","Nerve Net","Neural Networks Computer","Neurons","Periodicity","Spinal Cord"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"sparse firing in a hybrid central pattern generator for spinal motor circuits","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1162/neco_a_01660","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-735417","identifier":[{"id":"85191382409","type":"scopus"},{"id":"38658025","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-d8471105-fbc1-45ab-b1d8-55551d668440","ku-fe70a2e5-ce89-4ebb-9c7e-27717ac45eac"],"keyword":["Action Potentials","Animals","Central Pattern Generators","Computer Simulation","Humans","Models, Neurological","Nerve Net","Neural Networks, Computer","Neurons","Periodicity","Spinal Cord"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-75928F1C2BEDE4F1748BB6480F4CFD84"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/390818941/neco_a_01660.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1162/neco_a_01660","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/359292758/neco_a_01660.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical and Photonics Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical and Photonics Engineering, Automation and Control"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"drexel university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Drexel University","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Neuroscience, Molecular Neuroscience"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Beck","key":"strohmerpau","last":"Strohmer","locid":"9d84cc1d-55da-4a4a-8bac-79e9f0eadbda","name":"Strohmer, Beck","orcid":"0000-0002-8181-1977","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Elias","key":"najarropau","last":"Najarro","name":"Najarro, Elias","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jessica","key":"ausbornpau","last":"Ausborn","name":"Ausborn, Jessica","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Rune W.","key":"bergpau","last":"Berg","locid":"1f12a245-cbea-430c-9a19-9a440d1b33fc","name":"Berg, Rune W.","orcid":"0000-0001-6376-9368","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Silvia","ke